    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense looks primed for a productive outing, headlined by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who boasts the day\u2019s highest projection at 73.66. His matchup against Hughes is bolstered by an exceptional +14% park factor and a favorable platoon dynamic, making him an essential anchor in the utility spot. **Kyle Tucker** (71.48) and **Jacob Wilson** (68.63) follow closely, with **Kyle Tucker** benefiting from a high BvP efficiency rating against Nola and **Jacob Wilson** capitalizing on a soft matchup against Kelly (5.31 xERA) and the efficiency of the #1 spot in the lineup. **Drake Baldwin** rounds out our top-tier plays (66.52), as his high xwOBA and lead-off positioning position him to capitalize on the vulnerabilities of King.\n\nOur bench strategy remains disciplined, prioritizing daily efficiency over depth-chart standing. **Nasim Nunez** (53.28) stood as the most difficult omission; while his switch-hitting profile and favorable park factors were appealing, his projected bottom-of-the-order status (-8%) ultimately stifled his scoring potential compared to the high-leverage spots occupied by **Wade Meckler** and **Heliot Ramos**. We remain wary of **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s matchup against Rivera; despite his status as an elite bat, his score of 57.51 is suppressed by a negative platoon differential (-15%), highlighting the importance of the L/L disadvantage he faces today. Elsewhere, **Andy Pages** (65.40) is a high-upside play, as his elite BvP history against Nola effectively counters the quality of the opposing arm, though we are monitoring the threat of Nola's battery mate who may deter aggressive baserunning. \n\n**Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (58.12), **Coby Mayo** (59.21), and **Jackson Merrill** (57.47) occupy the middle-ground of our rotation, offering stable floors despite facing varying degrees of starter difficulty. While **Liam Hicks** (49.81) carries the lowest score in the starting lineup, his platoon advantage against Lambert provides enough situational juice to warrant a start over our deeper bench options. All managers should remain alert for late-breaking lineup changes, as any movement out of the top-six slots for **Wade Meckler** or **Brayan Rocchio** could necessitate a quick pivot to our available bench depth to maintain our category targets.",
